    "result_text": "The full build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature so `POST /api/owners` accepts an optional `title` (e.g. MR/MRS/MS/DR) and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `title` input property to the `OwnerFields` schema and a read-only `salutation` property to the `Owner` schema (these generate the `title` field on `OwnerFieldsDto` and `salutation` on `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `title` field mapped to a `title` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps `title` from `OwnerFieldsDto` into the entity on create.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `salutation(owner)` helper and wired it into `toOwnerDto` via `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", expression = \"java(salutation(owner))\")`, following the existing derived-field pattern (`displayName`, `initials`, etc.).\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table so the value persists across create\u2192read. Tests run on hsqldb.\n\nTest results: `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` passes (asserts `$.salutation == \"DR who\"`), and the full `./mvnw test` run is **BUILD SUCCESS** with no failures or errors.",
